2026-10-05T01:18:08.3708045Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-05T01:18:08.3719867Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-05T01:18:08.3721073Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-05T01:18:08.3721724Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-05T01:18:08.3722099Z 
2026-10-05T01:18:08.3722522Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-05T01:18:08.3722868Z 
2026-10-05T01:18:08.3723045Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-05T01:18:08.3723582Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-05T01:18:08.3723942Z 
2026-10-05T01:18:08.3724100Z If you would like to
2026-10-05T01:18:08.3724494Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-05T01:18:08.3724759Z 
2026-10-05T01:18:08.3725041Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-05T01:18:08.3725600Z   $ sh ./install-nix
